erged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nWhen trying to set a remote property's value using a non-remote object, it would result in the property being nullified. That's because non-remote objects are decoded into `EncodedObjectAsID` when passed to the remote, which contains an ID to an object that doesn't exist at runtime.\r\n\r\nThis PR makes so that if this is attempted, the remote will ignore the value, and instead it will summon an error toaster informing the user that is not allowed.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis PR grabs a little bit of code from #122510 to send the toaster request to the editor.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123395/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123395/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}